---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import ListeningLab from "../components/ListeningLab.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../site-config";
import "../styles/course.css";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Open Listening Lab"
  description="A small, inspectable sonification instrument for comparing pitch and rhythm mappings of the same dataset."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <header class="lab-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open instrument · teaching model</p>
    <p class="lab-lead">The numbers stay visible, the mapping changes while the source data stays fixed, and sound is never the only way to read the result. Use headphones at a comfortable level.</p>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Question</dt><dd>Where is the lowest region?</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Variable</dt><dd>Pitch or interval</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Constants</dt><dd>Values, order and timbre</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Task result, not preference</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>
  <h2>Explore the curve</h2>
  <ListeningLab />

  <section class="lab-protocol" aria-labelledby="protocol-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">A six-minute comparison</p>
    <h2 id="protocol-title">Run it like an experiment</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Listen blind</strong><span>Keep your eyes above the plot. Mark the sample range where you think the minimum occurs.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Inspect</strong><span>Read the ten values and compare your answer with samples 4–6.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Switch mapping</strong><span>Keep speed and level fixed. Repeat the same question in rhythm mode.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Change one constant</strong><span>Move the speed control and notice what changes in the experience but not in the source.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="interpretation-grid" aria-labelledby="interpretation-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Interpretation</p>
      <h2 id="interpretation-title">What each mapping can support</h2>
    </div>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Pitch</dt><dd>The minimum becomes a low note. Value order remains pitch order, but the musical meaning of “low” comes from the mapping.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Rhythm</dt><dd>The minimum creates the longest wait. The source was evenly sampled, so unequal playback time is a deliberate transformation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Neither</dt><dd>The ten values contain no uncertainty interval, provenance or discovered planet. This model cannot support an astronomical conclusion.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <h2>Limits of this demonstration</h2>
  <p>The curve is synthetic and has no uncertainty interval. It is useful for isolating one mapping decision, not for making an astronomical claim. Later labs add provenance, missing samples, error and real public datasets.</p>

  <p class="lab-next"><a href={withBase("/field-guide/")}>Record the comparison in the Sonification Field Guide</a>. Use the mapping ledger and listening-test sections so the result can be checked later.</p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .lab-intro { margin-block: 0 4rem; padding-block: 2rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--course-line-strong); }
  .lab-lead { max-width: 68ch; font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .lab-intro dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); margin: 2rem 0 0; border-block-start: 1px solid var(--at-border); }
  .lab-intro dl div { padding: 1rem 1rem 0 0; }
  .lab-intro dl div + div { padding-inline-start: 1rem; border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--at-border); }
  .lab-intro dt { color: var(--course-cyan); font-family: var(--at-font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lab-intro dd { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: var(--course-paper); font-weight: 600; }
  .lab-protocol { margin-block: 5rem; }
  .lab-protocol ol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--at-border); list-style: none; }
  .lab-protocol li { padding: 1.3rem; }
  .lab-protocol li + li { border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--at-border); }
  .lab-protocol strong, .lab-protocol span { display: block; }
  .lab-protocol strong { color: var(--course-gold); }
  .lab-protocol span { margin-block-start: 0.55rem; color: var(--at-text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .interpretation-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(15rem, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1.45fr); gap: 3rem; margin-block: 5rem; }
  .interpretation-grid h2 { color: var(--course-paper); }
  .interpretation-grid dl { margin: 0; }
  .interpretation-grid dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding-block: 1rem; border-block-end: 1px solid var(--at-divider); }
  .interpretation-grid dt { color: var(--course-coral); font-family: var(--at-font-mono); }
  .interpretation-grid dd { margin: 0; color: var(--at-text-secondary); }
  .lab-next { margin-block: 3rem; padding: 1.3rem; border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--course-gold); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--course-gold) 7%, transparent); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .lab-intro dl, .lab-protocol ol, .interpretation-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .lab-intro dl div + div, .lab-protocol li + li { border-block-start: 1px solid var(--at-border); border-inline-start: 0; }
    .lab-intro dl div + div { padding-inline-start: 0; }
  }
</style>
